--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI TripDetailPage at web parity: a pure @Observable
state holder (TripDetailPageModel — ADR-004, no networking in the view) over an
injectable TripDetailDataSource seam whose record value type mirrors the web `Trip`
1:1 (production binds the KMP `useTrip` → `GET /trips/{id}` repository through the
seam; the default SampleTripDetailDataSource seeds an API-response-shaped fixture so
the success state renders out of the box, and DEBUG Empty/Failing sources drive the
empty/error states).

NOTE on the web hook: `useTrip` is @deprecated on the web side — the backend has no
`GET /trips/{id}` route (only `GET /trips`), so the real-world outcome is the error
state, which the web surfaces gracefully through `PageContainer`'s error path. The
native page faithfully implements all four states regardless (loading/empty/error/
success), so it is correct whether the endpoint exists or 404s.

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title `Trip Detail` + dynamic
subtitle = the trip name, or `Trip #id`) and ALL FIVE manifest panels:

  Distance     — TSStatCard, value = fmtInt(convertDistanceFromSI(total_distance_m))
                 + the user's distance unit (km/mi/ft), via the shared `Units` facade.
  Energy-Used  — TSStatCard, value = fmtNumber(total_energy_wh) + "Wh" (pinned to Wh
                 exactly as the web hardcodes the unit; no energy-unit conversion).
  Efficiency   — TSStatCard, value = fmtInt(Wh / (m/1000), ×KM_PER_MILE when miles)
                 + "Wh/mi"|"Wh/km" (mirrors the web inline KM_PER_MILE precedent).
  Cost         — TSStatCard, value = formatCurrency(total_cost) (symbol + grouped
                 amount at the user's precision). No unit suffix, as the web omits it.
  GlassPanel5  — TSGlassPanel + TSKVList: Trip ID, Name, Started, Ended, Drives,
                 Charges (web `KVList` six rows; Name → '—' when null; Ended → '—'
                 when no end date; dates via medium-style formatDate parity).

Every absolute value is stored SI (metres, watt-hours) and converts only at the
SwiftUI render boundary through the shared `Units` facade (ADR-005) — nothing non-SI
is stored or computed. The four data states switch in place: loading (redacted
card/panel skeleton) / empty (ContentUnavailableView "Trip not found") / error
(TSErrorDisplay + Retry, never a blank region) / success (the five panels).

Adaptive across macOS/iPad (regular) + iPhone (compact): the stat grid is four
columns at regular width and two at compact width (web `cols={{ default: 2, lg: 4 }}`)
via the horizontal size class; the metadata panel scrolls. VoiceOver labels/values on
each stat card + the panel, Dynamic Type (token fonts), and light/dark via the P2
tokens. SwiftUI-native only — no web cloning, no WKWebView.

Navigation: the web detail deep-link /trips/:id maps to a typed NavigationDestination
— TripDetailRouteRegistration.swift declares `TripDetailLink(tripID:)` +
`.tripDetailDestination()` + a `make(tripID:)` factory, mirroring the sibling
DriveDetailRouteRegistration / ChargingDetailRouteRegistration shape, so any host
stack (the trips list, a separate parity unit) deep-links into one trip without
widening the value-less AppRoute enum. No other owners' files were edited.

i18n: every visible literal resolves from Localizable.xcstrings using the WEB key
names prefixed `translation.` (the established convention — cf. SignalDiffPage's
`translation.signalDiff.*`). All 12 `translation.trips.detail.*` keys ALREADY exist
in the catalog with English values, so ZERO new keys were added and the catalog is
untouched. Zero hardcoded user-facing strings.

